infographic sequence-snake-steps-underline-text
data
  title Six SLO alerting approaches — why five fail
  desc Each fixes the prior flaw; only Approach 6 survives
  sequences
    - label 1 · Error rate > threshold
      desc Too noisy — pages on any spike (alert fatigue)
    - label 2 · Add "for 5m" delay
      desc Kills brief spikes, but threshold still wrong
    - label 3 · Single burn rate, 1h window
      desc Catches outages, but long reset after fix
    - label 4 · Dual burn rate, OR logic
      desc OR fires on either — worst of both windows
    - label 5 · Dual severity, single windows
      desc Closer, but the page still has long reset
    - label 6 · MWMBR — long AND short
      desc Survives: rejects noise + clears in ~5 min
theme
  palette #f43f5e #f59e0b #6366f1 #14b8a6
